bounds — Explains type bounds written with `extends`.

Syntax:
  class Box<T extends Named> {
    value: T
  }
  
  class PairBox<T extends int | string> {
    value: T
  }
  
  function read<I extends Iterator<Item = string>>(it: I) -> I.Item? {
    return it.next()
  }

A bound constrains what type arguments are allowed and exposes members from the bound inside the generic body. Use `requires` for interface-to-interface prerequisites; use `extends` for generic parameter bounds and associated type bounds.
